l orientation\nStudentsafe Inbound University insurance\nVisa support\nStudy support\nContact International Student Experience\nHealth and safety\nRe-enrolling\nManaaki New Zealand Scholarships programme support\nHome\nInternational\nApply and enrol\nHow to apply\nInternational\nTe Kahupapa ki Tai / International\nStudy options\nUndergraduate degrees\nPostgraduate programmes\nYour postgraduate study options\nPhD\nStudy Abroad and Exchange\nFoundation Studies\nPathways\nNorthern Consortium UK\nEnglish for Academic Purposes\nWhy study in Wellington\nGraduate employability\nConnect with Wellington\nLiving in Wellington\nDiscover Wellington\nExplore your campuses\nWorking in New Zealand\nMoney and banking\nHealthcare\nBringing your family\nSupport for international students\nVisa and insurance support\nArrival meeting service\nInternational buddy programme\nHealth, safety, and wellbeing\nStudy support\nStudents under 18 years\nInformation sessions\nHello Wellington\u2014India roadshow\nInternational stories\nVisit us in Wellington\nScholarships and fees\nInternational Scholarships\nInternational Scholarships update\nManaaki New Zealand Scholarships Programme\nYour Scholarship experience\nWhat the Scholarship covers\nApply for a Manaaki New Zealand Scholarship\nScholarship study options\nGet ready for your Scholarship\nOrganise your travel\nWhen you first arrive\nMeet our Scholarships team\nFunding for international study\nUS Federal Student Aid\nEligibility\nLoan types\nApplication process\nCost of attendance\nSatisfactory Academic Progress\nReturn of Title IV Funds\nManage and repay your loan\nStudent consumer information\nGlossary\nSallie Mae private loans\nVeterans Affairs Education Benefits\nCost calculator\nYour fees and costs\nPaying your fees\nHow to pay your fees\nApply and enrol\nEntry requirements\nEnglish Language requirements\nStandard undergraduate English requirements\nStandard postgraduate English requirements\nProgrammes with higher English requirements\nProgrammes with external English requirements\nDates and deadlines\nHow to apply\nPrepare your documents\nApply as a New Zealand secondary school student\nP\u016baha\u2014log in or sign up\nYour Offer\nEnrol for courses\nChoosing your courses\nCredit transfer and exemptions\nFind an agent\nApplication and enrolment terms and conditions\nPrepare to study\nYour offer\nEnrol for courses\nDates and deadlines\nStudent visa\nAccommodation\nAccommodation for Scholarship students\nInsurance\nStudentsafe University insurance\nInternational buddy programme\nCheck your health needs\nCourse planning\nPreparing for travel\nArrival meeting service\nInternational Orientation\nOrientation and start dates\nTimetable\nCurrent international students\nInternational orientation\nStudentsafe Inbound University insurance\nVisa support\nStudy support\nContact International Student Experience\nHealth and safety\nRe-enrolling\nManaaki New Zealand Scholarships programme support\nHow to apply\nFollow these steps to apply for a degree or other qualification, pathway programme, or study abroad programme at Victoria University of Wellington.\nThis guide is for new international students applying for undergraduate or postgraduate qualifications, excluding doctorates.\nThere is separate guidance if you are:\napplying as a New Zealand secondary school student\napplying to do a PhD or other doctorate; apply via the Faculty of Graduate Research\napplying as an agent or partner, on behalf of a student; apply via the Agent and Partner Portal\napplying for Foundation Studies\u2014The Victoria University of Wellington Foundation Studies Programme is taught exclusively through UP International College New Zealand. Apply via the UP Education website.\n1. Choose what to study, and check the details\nEach of our qualifications and major subjects has a webpage that provides an overview, a list of the courses you need to do to complete the programme (\u2018requirements\u2019), and what you need to be accepted (\u2018entry requirements\u2019). Use the switcher at the top right of the qualification or subject webpage to show information applicable to you, depending on your nationality.\nBefore you start your application, make sure you check:\nthe application and start dates\nfees and costs.\nChoose your programme\n2. Check that you meet University entry requirements\nTo study at the University, you\u2019ll need to meet our English language and academic entry requirements. Check that you meet these before you apply.\nCheck entry requirements\nIf you don\u2019t meet the entry requirements\nWe are here to help you meet your study goals. If you don\u2019t meet the entry requirements for:\nEnglish language\u2014 you can apply for our English for Academic Purposes programme.\nundergraduate study\u2014 you can apply for our Foundation Studies programme.\npostgraduate study\u2014 you can talk to us. We can help you build a pathway to your degree.\n3. Prepare your documentation\nYou will need to show us proof that you meet the entry requirements for your chosen programme.\nWhen you apply, you need to provide certified copies of your original documents. If your documents aren\u2019t in English, you\u2019ll also need to provide certified translations.\nFind out more about certifying documents\n4. Apply online\nApply by our application deadlines to make sure you have enough time to apply for a student visa and accommodation before you travel to New Zealand.\nYou can apply for undergraduate, postgraduate, English for Academic Purposes, and Study Abroad programmes via P\u016baha, our student portal. You\u2019ll need a personal email address to start your online application.\nYou\u2019ll need to know what you want to study (your degree or other qualification) and when you want to start studying (the year and trimester) before you start your application.\nMake sure you read the terms and conditions when you apply\nYou can also get an agent to apply on your behalf\nFind an agent\nStart your application Find out more about how to access P\u016baha\n5. Check your emails\nWe will send you an email to confirm we have received your application. We\u2019ll then email you to confirm whether your application is successful, usually within one week (undergraduate) or three to four weeks (postgraduate). Some programmes may take longer to assess due to interview, thesis, and audition requirements.\n6. Prepare to study\nOnce you have an Offer of Place, we\u2019ll tell you everything you need to know about preparing for your studies, including how to enrol for your courses, and pay your fees.\nPrepare to study\nNeed help to apply?\nContact us or seek the help of an approved agent if you have any questions about applying.\nRelated links\nTerms and conditions for applying and enrolling\nApplication deadlines\nRelated links\nPrepare your documents\nP\u016baha\u2014log in or sign up\nConnect with us\nContact us\nFind an agent\nInformation sessions\nGet a student guide\nEmergencies\nFaculties\nArchitecture and Design Innovation\nBusiness and Government\nEducation, Health, and Psychological Sciences\nGraduate Research\nHumanities and Social Sciences\nLaw\nScience and Engineering\nContacts and directories\nStaff directory\nMedia enquiries\nFind a researcher\nHealth and safety\nCampuses\nKelburn Campus\nPipitea Campus\nTe Aro Campus\nAuckland Premises\nStudy\nProgrammes and courses\nApply and enrol\nScholarships\nAccommodation\nSchools hub\nStudents\nLibrary\nServices and support\nFinancial survival\nKey dates\nCourses\nP\u016baha\u2014Student portal\nNuku\u2014Learning environment\nLibrary\nStaff\nStaff email\nStaff Service Centre\nMyTools for staff\nTeaching support\nWorking here\nCurrent vacancies\nAlumni\nStay connected\nGiving\nDonate\nLatest news\nEvents\nResearch expertise\nPublications\nSocial media\n0800 04 04 04\n+64 4 472 1000\ninfo@vuw.ac.nz\nEmergency: 0800 842 8888\nSite info\nSite map\nFeedback\nGlossary\nPrivacy\nCopyright \u00a9 Victoria University of Wel